{"seq":3,"gate":"premortem","ts":"2026-09-07T00:53:02.644Z","ticket":"T286","data":{"promptOnly":true,"usageStatus":"unreported","verdict":"{\n  \"causes\": [\n    {\n      \"cause\": \"The extraction cached a container table or standing result, allowing a revoked binding to remain admitted.\",\n      \"earliest_signal\": \"The same Gateway and binding still pass after the signed revocation is applied.\",\n      \"prevention\": \"Read live authority on every call and test success followed by revocation and refusal without rebuilding the Gateway.\",\n      \"interrogation_question\": \"Does the revocation test reuse the same Gateway and binding while an independent connection remains authorized?\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"cause\": \"connectionStands checked only the bound container declaration and overlooked a removed ancestor whose descendant and inbox survived.\",\n      \"earliest_signal\": \"A descendant binding passes after its parent's declaration is struck.\",\n      \"prevention\": \"Preserve chainBreaksAt over the declared parent chain and retain a descendant fixture with a surviving inbox grant.\",\n      \"interrogation_question\": \"Does the ancestor-removal test leave the bound descendant and its write grant intact so that only the chain check can refuse?\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"cause\": \"boundChannelAdmits omitted openerStands(channel), and matching inbox identity admitted an incompatible openedBy.\",\n      \"earliest_signal\": \"A valid binding with matching openedFrom and incompatible openedBy passes.\",\n      \"prevention\": \"Keep the explicit incompatible-opener control with all earlier predicates satisfied.\",\n      \"interrogation_question\": \"Does that control also retain receive leeway so refusal isolates the channel opener check?\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"cause\": \"The receive check used binding.container instead of channel.into, retaining channel authority after destination receive leeway was withdrawn.\",\n      \"earliest_signal\": \"A channel remains admitted when its destination loses receive leeway but the binding stays standing.\",\n      \"prevention\": \"Preserve receivesNow on the current container table and channel destination, with independent leeway withdrawal.\",\n      \"interrogation_question\": \"Does the withdrawal fixture distinguish the channel destination from the binding container and prove the binding still stands?\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"cause\": \"A convenience Gateway operation inside the shared probe created or repaired state while checking authority.\",\n      \"earliest_signal\": \"Primary or attached inbox delta histories change after a successful or refused probe.\",\n      \"prevention\": \"Retain the existing read-only helper composition and compare complete primary and attached inbox histories around both outcomes.\",\n      \"interrogation_question\": \"Are all fixture mutations completed before snapshots, and are both storage locations checked after each probe?\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"cause\": \"HTTP integration changed the unbound federateAdmits branch or left callers using a duplicate private implementation.\",\n      \"earliest_signal\": \"Unbound grant behavior changes, or HTTP still contains a separate connectionStands implementation after extraction.\",\n      \"prevention\": \"Replace the private checks with imports, preserve the unbound branch text and arguments, and inspect every existing call site alongside server regression results.\",\n      \"interrogation_question\": \"Does the integration diff preserve the unbound branch and route every previous connection check through the shared function?\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"cause\": \"The new module's missing-import failure was recorded as proof of a newly failing authority behavior, overstating what the frozen rail established.\",\n      \"earliest_signal\": \"Evidence labels the module-absence red as a revocation or isolation regression despite baseline controls passing.\",\n      \"prevention\": \"Record the red as API extraction, freeze the authored test hash, and separately record baseline and implemented behavior results.\",\n      \"interrogation_question\": \"Does the evidence distinguish module availability from independently exercised authority semantics?\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"cause\": \"A later consumer treated these booleans as a complete renderer context and served unscoped data or enabled ambient signing after a successful check.\",\n      \"earliest_signal\": \"T286 completion is cited as sufficient authorization for renderer activation or unrestricted Gateway access.\",\n      \"prevention\": \"Keep renderer activation, scoped serving, exact identity, durability, and signing authority outside this extraction and require their separate implementation review.\",\n      \"interrogation_question\": \"Do completion records state that these functions preserve existing authority predicates without supplying a renderer data or signing context?\"\n    }\n  ]\n}","specPath":"/tmp/loam-t278-evidence/T286-spec.md"},"files":{"/tmp/loam-t278-evidence/T286-spec.md":"8b6b6a7805ff39c1c9b1b56507144fa84153f62ed3ac720a8de68ff478990b4c"},"prev":"3237ddaa3c43d546e7dd78a5959b56b05e7f84ac14ff5705f4db43d7ba0024a1","sig":"ad088de218d442e55406989a2d6f487f4d4af7a5fbe4cab5a9bd2c92b2b6cb0a"}
